Date: Mon, 10 Jun 2024 18:31:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0950/1695] drivers: stm32_risab: handle differently RISAB base
 address

Add risab_base() helper to get a RISAB virtual base address and store
a struct io_pa_va in stm32_risab_pdata.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 1ea658a5ea1fd0e3a28780ec24d53bef0370ca11 drivers: stm32_risab: handle differently RISAB base address]
Change-Id: I5bd78ba8c1c5c7be9c5c442705ead6568d63bbef
Signed-off-by: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/389861
Reviewed-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
Tested-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c | 76 ++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
index 011d78879..51d4b4609 100644
--- a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
+++ b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
@@ -82,8 +82,8 @@ struct stm32_risab_pdata {
 	struct clk *clock;
 	struct mem_region region_cfged;
